    <title>
        <en>Utilities &amp; Waste Management</en>
    </title>
    <description>
        <en><![CDATA[Farms trade electricity, slurry and manure with each other through invoices.

Open the Utilities page in the ESC menu. The farm manager can send a bill (to sell) or an order (to buy) to another farm; that farm's manager accepts or declines it. Set the amount, or take everything the seller has in stock, and set your own price per 1,000 liters (the game's price is shown as a guide). Trade once, or every day or every week until either farm ends it.

Electricity goes straight from the seller's power-producing productions into the buyer's productions the buyer picked, and is paid for as it arrives. Slurry and manure are paid for up front and collected by anyone on the buying farm: drive up to the seller's slurry pit, manure heap or silo and load as usual, and only what you paid for is offered. The liters come out of the seller's own stock. Buyers can reserve what they paid for, so the seller can't use it. Liters that are never collected are refunded when the invoice ends.

Multiplayer: everything runs on the server and only farm managers can trade.]]></en>
    </description>
    <iconFilename>icon_UtilitiesWasteManagement.dds</iconFilename>
    <multiplayer supported="true" />

